Z||000000||Bluemagic||03-14-2001||06:10 AM||||Iwant to do a notchback to fastback conversion on my 85   but cant find a donor  car  or the parts,is there any one in the miami or surrounding area who has one that is not too expensive also which is more practical from a cost and effort stand point  V8 or 3800 conversion need some feed back thanks.||||reg||3
Z||000001||KRMFiero||03-14-2001||08:37 AM||||Welcome to the forum!<P>Okay, The notchback to Fastback conversion from what i hear is very easy, I wanted to do this conversion on my 84 but i havent found a doner car in my area eather. <P>cheak out <A HREF="http://www.usedfieroparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.usedfieroparts.com/</A>  i think they have a conversion kit I forgot where they are located though.<P><BR>about the 3800/v-8 swap,  I would rather have a 3800 Series II SC engine, they rev nice, very quick, good power but the only thing is there are ALOT more electronics to hook up and stuff. I currently in the procces of putting a 4.5L caddy v-8 in my 84 Fiero, but its just taking awhile because i dont have alot of money.   If you have the money i would go for the 3800, if you dont have alot of money go for the 4.X Caddy. I would not put a small block chevy in, they weigh alot more, and you would have a better chance of blowing your tranny      but its up to you<P>cheak out: <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx</A> <P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||03-14-2001||09:59 AM||||Welcome to the forum! Wanna join the Palm Beach club?? Not so far from you.<BR>Check <A HREF="http://www.coparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.coparts.com</A>  . You may find a donor there and order the parts from the junk yard. I did it for a Vette & works.||||reg||1
