Z||000004||Bluemagic||03-15-2001||01:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>Welcome to the forum!<P>Okay, The notchback to Fastback conversion from what i hear is very easy, I wanted to do this conversion on my 84 but i havent found a doner car in my area eather. <P>cheak out <A HREF="http://www.usedfieroparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.usedfieroparts.com/</A>  i think they have a conversion kit I forgot where they are located though.<P><BR>about the 3800/v-8 swap,  I would rather have a 3800 Series II SC engine, they rev nice, very quick, good power but the only thing is there are ALOT more electronics to hook up and stuff. I currently in the procces of putting a 4.5L caddy v-8 in my 84 Fiero, but its just taking awhile because i dont have alot of money.   If you have the money i would go for the 3800, if you dont have alot of money go for the 4.X Caddy. I would not put a small block chevy in, they weigh alot more, and you would have a better chance of blowing your tranny      but its up to you<P>cheak out: <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx</A> <P>Kyle<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Idid check out the site and decided to go the caddy route||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jonathan||03-15-2001||09:15 AM||||I bought everything for my Fastback conversion from Ed Parks @ the Fiero Factory in Toney Alabama.  I already had the body off so the conversion was easy.  I have had the car painted but have not put in sail panels yet.  Check it out at my website.   <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/nc2/jpfiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank>www.angelfire.com/nc2/jpfiero/index.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fierotag2.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000006||Turbo1dr||03-15-2001||11:59 AM||||Keep looking around to find a donor car. I found a 86 GT at a local salvage yard for $500. It even had aftermarket aluminum rims! I've already done the conversion to my 86 SE.  <P>------------------<BR>86 SE Fiero (Buick Turbo V6 transplant in progress)<P><B>78 Malibu</B> 3.8L Turbo Buick<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Homex.html" TARGET=_blank>TURBO WONDER</A><BR>Best 8th: 1.548, 6.62@106.32  3450lb<BR>TE-70 3 bolt, Ported Stock Iron Heads and Intake<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Modifications_files/Intercooler.jpg" TARGET=_blank>2.5 stock intercoolers</A><BR>Vernon Swindell, Jr.||||reg||6
